-- Tests for bc-interpretation-terms.l4: one block per defined-term entry of the Interpretation Act (British Columbia),
-- RSBC 1996, c. 238 (ss 1, 8.1(1), 29, 29.1(1), 29.2, 32(1)), generated by `gen-terms.py` from `terms-data.py`.
-- For each entry: how it defines, each thing it names (TRUE), each thing it leaves out (FALSE), a thing it does not
-- list (FALSE if the list is closed, a refusal if it is open), the Acts it points at, the conditions it carries.
-- The cross-reference entries of s 29 are checked: where each sends the reader, and that the target is defined.
-- The expected values come from the curated reading in `terms-data.py`, which the encoder made from the text; they are
-- not computed from the L4 (NOTES.md, finding 8 says what that check does and does not show).
-- Hand-written tests of the same module, with expected values written beside them from the text, are in
-- `bc-tests-terms-rules.l4`.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bc-interpretation-terms`

§ `The catalogue, entry by entry`

-- >>> GENERATED by gen-terms.py: one block per entry
-- s 1 definition of Act (src:10)
